1956		rewritten over the mixture of product distributions
1957		$D_{\mathrm{v},i} \times D_{\mathrm{v},j}$ with $z$ uniformly random on
1958		$\ell_Z$, and, since
1959		$T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z,z}_{b}
1960		= \E_{x \in \ell_X} \sum_a
1961		T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z}
1962		_{[\mathrm{eval}_x(\cdot)=a,\ \mathrm{eval}_z(\cdot)=b]}$,
1963		one may additionally average over $x$ uniformly random on $\ell_X$. Up
1964		to error $m(\sqrt{\delta_P} + \sqrt{\delta_Q})$ --- obtained by
1965		applying the error inflation of
1966		Lemma~\ref{lem:restricted-line-mixture-bounds} to the conclusion of
1967		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-xz-lines} (transported to the sub-line distribution
1968		via Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-sublines}) and to the consistency relations of
1969		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-10} --- the resulting quantity is close to
1970		$\E \sum_{a,b} \bra{\hat\psi}
